  "description": "VEDDUH crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C62 H78 Dy6 N8 O32,2(C1 H4 O1),3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.591-3.992 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.88-112.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C62H78Dy6N8O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
